-create a simple pojo class?
-pojo: plain old style java object
-pojo class have varibles, methods, these methods will be getter and setters
-getter and setter are special methods to either get the value of the class or set the value
-what happends behind the scene when u create a object of a class?
-there are 2 types of memory stack mem and heap memory
-Person obj=new Person();  after doing this ,
-a variable called obj , will be storedi n the stack of main()
-since stack is LIFO, it will
-this stack is created in the heap memory

- Person q;
- will not creat a object since it does not hvae new keyword and not reffering to anything hence

- new Person(); will allocate memory but have no reference
- java performs automatic garbage collection
- it checks if there are any objects which has no refrence. and deletes it

-Person q=new Person()
-Person p=q
-shallow copy is when 2 references point to same memory
- 2 refrences are pointing to same memory hence they share the same memory

-Person p=new Person()
-Person q=new Person()
-deep copy is when 2 refferences are having different memory , hence they dont share memory

-ultimately , when you do Person p=new Person();
-new Person() allocated memory in a heap, where it created a stack which has its methods, varibales (added by the constructor )
-Person p is a reference of type Person.

